From a66fce391080ff62e60de3766ff1ad51857ff6ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 17:06:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: keep the swizzle when a source modifier folds

A swizzled source loses its swizzle as soon as a negate or an absolute value
is applied to it:

  v_in.wzyx * 0.5      MULADDv  export0 = C0.xxxx,  R0.wzyx, C0.xxxx
  -v_in.wzyx * 0.5     MULADDv  export0 = C0.xxxx, -R0,      C0.xxxx
  abs(v_in.wzyx)       MULADDv  export0 = C0.xxxx, |R0|,     C0.xxxx

The components read are whatever the register happens to hold in order, so
the result is wrong wherever the swizzle was not the identity.

The modifier is folded by chasing past the fneg or fabs to the value
underneath, and that intermediate instruction carried a swizzle of its own.
nir_legacy_chase_alu_src() composes the two and hands back the result, but we
built the swizzle from the original source, which by then describes only the
modifier's own trivially swizzled result.

Build it from the chased source instead:

  -v_in.wzyx * 0.5     MULADDv  export0 = C0.xxxx, -R0.wzyx,  C0.xxxx
  abs(v_in.wzyx)       MULADDv  export0 = C0.xxxx, |R0.wzyx|, C0.xxxx

This reaches much further than the obvious abs() and negate cases.  ceil()
lowers to fneg(ffloor(fneg(a))) and mod() to a - b * floor(a / b), so both
fold a modifier over a swizzled source, and the inverse trigonometric
functions are built the same way.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43606>

---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c
index a3d0abcf1d9..9ea93355adf 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c
@@ -430,17 +430,20 @@ emit_alu(struct ir2_context *ctx, nir_alu_instr *alu)
    for (int i = 0; i < info->num_inputs; i++) {
       nir_alu_src *src = &alu->src[i];
 
-      /* compress swizzle with writemask when applicable */
+      nir_legacy_alu_src legacy_src =
+         nir_legacy_chase_alu_src(src, true /* fuse_abs */);
+
+      /* compress swizzle with writemask when applicable.  Take it from the
+       * chased source: folding a neg or an abs skips over an instruction that
+       * carried a swizzle of its own, and only the chase composes the two.
+       */
       unsigned swiz = 0, j = 0;
       for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
          if (!(legacy_dest.write_mask & 1 << i) && !info->output_size)
             continue;
-         swiz |= swiz_set(src->swizzle[i], j++);
+         swiz |= swiz_set(legacy_src.swizzle[i], j++);
       }
 
-      nir_legacy_alu_src legacy_src =
-         nir_legacy_chase_alu_src(src, true /* fuse_abs */);
-
       instr->src[i] = make_legacy_src(ctx, legacy_src.src);
       instr->src[i].swizzle = swiz_merge(instr->src[i].swizzle, swiz);
       instr->src[i].negate = legacy_src.fneg;

